import sys
p = sys.argv[1]
lines = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read().split('\n')
idx = [i for i, l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith('| 666 |')]
assert len(idx) == 1
lines.insert(idx[0] + 1, "| 667 | 2026-10-26 | **Minor Scales, chapter 22 (Build AC; the board's call 6 as the syllabus settles it).** Built on row 666. A room after Key Signatures on the second Prelim - Grade 1 floor: the minor key on paper and by ear, as the Grade 1 theory asks. Five steps with pads: (1) Major or minor third: count the half steps on the keys (4 or 3), hear them one after the other and together, 'Which one?'. (2) The minor key's key signature: A (none), E (F#), D (Bb), G (Bb Eb), three half steps below the major (counted 3 2 1 on the keys); name the minor from a key signature. (3) The harmonic minor: the staff (SkgStaff with the major's key signature; treble or bass, the bass within one ledger line) and the keys; the raised 7th written beside the note; 'which note goes up?'. (4) Tone, semitone, tone and a half: mark each step of a harmonic minor (T S T T S T1/2 S), the half steps counted on the keys. (5) Major or harmonic minor by ear (C G F D Bb major; A E D G harmonic minor). Drill: six levels (third by sight, third by ear, name the minor key, the raised 7th, T/S/T1/2, scale by ear). Home: Pitch -> Scales now has three groups: Major scales (its nine lessons, check Scales), Minor scales (the five new lessons and 'Three kinds of minor', check Minor Scales), More scales (pentatonic). Book: 7 pages. Not yet: Workbook and teacher's copy; i and V in a minor key (Chords). Files: drills.html, drills.src.html, _workspace/concept-book-kit/sc/patch691.py (+ msx.jsx, msh.jsx). |")
open(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write('\n'.join(lines)); print('ok')
